atom     numeric/transcendental-correctly-rounded
source   curated
kind     accuracy — where the reference is measurably the less correct engine

# The generated method matrix records 49 cells where the two engines return
# doubles differing in the last place. They are not a rendering difference: the
# doubles differ. Checked against the correctly-rounded IEEE-754 result, rakupp
# is exact in every one and the reference is 1-3 ULP out.
#
# This is the case the oracle-is-not-the-arbiter rule exists for. Mathematics
# decides a correctly-rounded result, not an implementation, so the assertion is
# the exact value and the ruling is recorded against the reference.

- id     0001
  from   review:2026-08-16 · generated/types/methods-Int.grid
  code   (1).asinh
  is     0.881373587019543e0
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → 0.8813735870195429e0
  oracle rakupp-3.14.0 → 0.881373587019543e0
  verdict impl-bug
  why    asinh(1) = ln(1+sqrt 2); the correctly-rounded double is 0.881373587019543, and the reference is one ULP below it
  ruled  2026-08-16 against rakudo-2026.07

